CHANGE ENTRY #2
Date: 2025-07-30
Topic: Bug Fix — Backend Crash on Startup (database.py)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  The Flask app crashed at startup when PostgreSQL was unreachable because
  SQLAlchemy engine and session factory were created eagerly at module import
  time. Fixed by making both lazy.

FILE MODIFIED:

  backend/database.py  [FIXED]

  BEFORE:
    engine = create_engine(DATABASE_URL, ...)          # ran at import time
    SessionLocal = sessionmaker(bind=engine, ...)      # ran at import time

  AFTER:
    _engine = None
    _session_factory = None

    def _get_engine():
        global _engine
        if _engine is None:
            _engine = create_engine(DATABASE_URL, ...)
        return _engine

    def _get_session_factory():
        global _session_factory
        if _session_factory is None:
            _session_factory = sessionmaker(bind=_get_engine(), ...)
        return _session_factory

  - Base = declarative_base() kept at module level (safe — no DB connection).
  - is_available() updated to call _get_engine() inside try/except.
  - get_session() updated to use _get_session_factory().

  IMPACT:
    - App no longer crashes at startup when Postgres is unreachable.
    - DB connection is only attempted when the first actual DB operation runs.
    - Alembic env.py confirmed to only import Base and DATABASE_URL (not engine)
      — no breakage to migrations.

