CHANGE ENTRY #3
Date: 2025-07-30
Topic: Bug Fix — CSS Conflict on Login/Signup (LandingPage.jsx)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  Login and signup forms had broken styling because LandingPage imported
  LoginPage and rendered it as a child inside its own wrapper div, causing
  the landing page's CSS (nav, blob animations, background) to bleed into
  the auth form. Fixed by inlining the auth form directly in LandingPage.

FILE MODIFIED:

  frontend/src/LandingPage.jsx  [FIXED]

  BEFORE:
    - Imported LoginPage component.
    - Rendered: if (showLogin) return <LoginPage />
    - LoginPage was returned as a child inside LandingPage's component tree,
      meaning React rendered it inside <div className="landing-page"> with
      all landing page styles bleeding in.

  AFTER:
    - Removed import LoginPage entirely.
    - Added openAuth(mode) function — sets showAuth=true, initialises mode
      ('login' or 'register').
    - Added switchMode(mode) function — switches between login/register tabs.
    - Auth form inlined directly using useAuth() for login/register calls.
    - When showAuth=true, renders <div className="auth-shell"> as a full
      clean replacement (not nested inside landing wrapper).
    - AUTH_STYLES constant added — holds all auth-specific CSS injected via
      <style> tag, fully isolated from landing page styles.
    - "← Back to home" button added to return to landing page without
      refreshing.
    - All nav/CTA buttons updated:
        setShowLogin(true)  →  openAuth('login')
        setShowLogin(true)  →  openAuth('register')  (for sign-up CTAs)

  SIDE EFFECTS:
    - frontend/src/App.jsx: removed unused import LoginPage.
    - frontend/src/LoginPage.jsx: file still exists on disk but is now
      unreferenced by any component. Can be deleted in a future cleanup.

