CHANGE ENTRY #4
Date: 2025-07-30
Topic: Bug Fix — ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED on /api/auth/register (Vite proxy)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  Browser was hitting http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register directly and
  getting ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED. Root cause: no Vite dev-server proxy was
  configured, so the browser made the request directly to port 5000 instead
  of going through Vite. Fixed by adding a proxy in vite.config.js and
  switching AuthContext to use relative URLs.

FILES MODIFIED:

  frontend/vite.config.js  [MODIFIED]
  - BEFORE: server block had only port and host.
  - AFTER:  Added proxy block:
              '/api' → target: VITE_API_BASE_URL || 'http://localhost:5000'
              changeOrigin: true
  - IMPACT: All /api/* requests from the browser are now forwarded by Vite's
            dev server to the backend, avoiding direct cross-origin calls.

  frontend/src/AuthContext.jsx  [MODIFIED]
  - BEFORE: const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL || 'http://localhost:5000'
  - AFTER:  const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL || ''
  - IMPACT: When no env var is set (local dev), axios uses relative URLs
            (e.g. /api/auth/register) which Vite's proxy forwards correctly.
            In production/Docker, VITE_API_BASE_URL can still be set to an
            absolute URL and it will be used as-is.

NOTE:
  ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED also means the backend Docker container may not be
  running. Always verify with: docker compose ps
  Start if needed with:        docker compose up -d
  Check backend logs with:     docker compose logs backend --tail=50


