CHANGE ENTRY #5
Date: 2025-07-30
Topic: Bug Fix — Alembic DuplicateTable error on backend startup
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  Backend crashed on startup with:
    sqlalchemy.exc.ProgrammingError: (psycopg2.errors.DuplicateTable)
    relation "series" already exists
  The tables (series, datasets, series_versions, series_row_values) were
  created before Alembic managed them, so the DB had no alembic_version row.
  On startup, alembic upgrade head tried to CREATE TABLE series and failed.

FILES MODIFIED:

  backend/entrypoint.sh  [MODIFIED]
  - BEFORE: ran `alembic upgrade head` with set -e (any failure = crash).
  - AFTER:  runs `alembic upgrade head`; if it fails (DuplicateTable),
            falls back to `alembic stamp head` which records the current
            migration as applied without running any DDL.
  - IMPACT: Backend no longer crashes when tables already exist from a
            previous run before Alembic managed them.

  backend/alembic/versions/20260729_0000_0002_create_series_datasets_tables.py  [MODIFIED]
  - BEFORE: each op.create_table() ran unconditionally.
  - AFTER:  added sa.inspect(bind).get_table_names() check before each
            create_table call — skips creation if the table already exists.
  - IMPACT: Migration 0002 is now fully idempotent. Safe to run against
            both fresh databases and databases that already have these tables.


