CHANGE ENTRY #10
Date: 2025-08-03
Topic: Bug Fix — EDA Modal isAR Condition Always False (Invoice Cards Never Shown)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  The three invoice amount cards (Source Total Invoice Amount, Target Total
  Invoice Amount, Difference) were never rendered in the EDA modal even after
  Entry #9 added them. Root cause: the condition used to decide whether to show
  the AR financial path was:

    const isAR = payload.dataType === 'transactional' && arResult?.summary;

  payload.dataType comes from buildPayload() → report.data_type, which is set
  by the standard diff engine (difference_summary / transactional_difference_summary).
  The AR reconcile run is a completely separate flow — it does NOT update
  payload.dataType. So the condition was always false when opening the EDA modal
  from the day-by-day scoreboard, because arResult is only populated after an
  explicit AR run, not after a standard series comparison.

WHY THIS MATTERS:
  The EDA modal is opened from the scoreboard (series flow). The series flow
  uses the standard diff engine, not the AR engine. arResult?.summary is only
  truthy if the user also ran an AR reconcile in the same session. So the
  original condition required BOTH a transactional series AND an AR run — an
  unlikely combination that was never tested.

FIX:
  Changed to:
    const isAR = !!(arResult?.summary);

  This means: show the AR financial section whenever an AR result is in state,
  regardless of what payload.dataType says. The AR run is the authoritative
  signal that AR data exists.

FILE MODIFIED:
  frontend/src/App.jsx  [FIXED]
  - BEFORE: const isAR = payload.dataType === 'transactional' && arResult?.summary;
  - AFTER:  const isAR = !!(arResult?.summary);
  - IMPACT: Invoice amount cards now render correctly in the EDA modal whenever
            an AR reconcile has been run in the current session.

