CHANGE ENTRY #11
Date: 2025-08-03
Topic: Feature — EDA Modal Data Type Badge + Invoice Totals for Standard Transactional Series
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  After Entry #10 fixed the AR path, a new problem was identified: the EDA modal
  showed "Master Data" badge and master-data KPIs even for series that were
  created as transactional data (without running an AR reconcile). Two issues:

  1. The badge in the top-right of the EDA modal header was hardcoded to show
     "Master Data" / "⚡ AR / Transactional" based only on isAR (AR run done),
     not on the actual data type of the series.

  2. For transactional series (standard diff engine, no AR run), there were no
     invoice financial totals shown at all — the AR financial section only
     appears when arResult exists.

WHY:
  The standard transactional diff engine (transactional_difference_summary in
  app.py) did not compute any invoice totals. It only produced row-level diff
  data. The EDA modal had no way to show financial totals for these series.

SOLUTION — TWO-PART FIX:

  Part A: Backend — compute invoice_summary in transactional_difference_summary
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FILE MODIFIED: backend/app.py  [MODIFIED]

  Added invoice total computation at the end of transactional_difference_summary(),
  just before the return statement:

    # Detect amount column and compute invoice totals for transactional EDA
    amount_keywords = ("amount", "amt", "value", "total", "price", "sum", "debit", "credit")
    amount_col = next(
        (c for c in df_source.columns
         if any(w in c.lower() for w in amount_keywords) and c in df_target.columns),
        None
    )
    invoice_summary = None
    if amount_col:
        def _to_float_series(s):
            return pd.to_numeric(
                s.astype(str).str.replace(r'[\$,]', '', regex=True), errors='coerce'
            )
        src_total = float(_to_float_series(df_source[amount_col]).sum())
        tgt_total = float(_to_float_series(df_target[amount_col]).sum())
        invoice_summary = {
            "amount_column": amount_col,
            "source_invoice_total": round(src_total, 2),
            "target_invoice_total": round(tgt_total, 2),
            "invoice_difference": round(src_total - tgt_total, 2),
        }

  The return dict now includes "invoice_summary": invoice_summary.

  Logic:
  - Scans source column names for amount-like keywords (case-insensitive).
  - Requires the column to also exist in target (same name after alignment).
  - Strips $ and , before parsing to float (handles formatted currency strings).
  - Sums ALL rows (not grouped) so every transaction line is counted.
  - Returns None if no amount column is found (safe — UI checks for null).

  Part B: Frontend — isTransactional flag + invoice section for non-AR path
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FILE MODIFIED: frontend/src/App.jsx  [MODIFIED]

  Added isTransactional derived from payload.dataType:
    const isTransactional = payload.dataType === 'transactional' || !!(arResult?.summary);
    const isAR = !!(arResult?.summary);

  - isTransactional: true if the series was stored as transactional OR if an
    AR run has been done. Controls which KPI strip and summary section to show.
  - isAR: true only when an AR run result is in state. Controls whether to show
    the full AR financial section (with AR-specific KPIs and pie chart).

  EDA modal non-AR transactional branch now shows:
    1. Standard 7-cell KPI strip (Total, Matched, Updated, Inserted, Missing,
       Duplicate, Quality) — same as before.
    2. NEW: Invoice Financial Summary section (only when invoice_summary exists
       in the report OR can be computed from full_comparison rows):
         - Source Total Invoice Amount  (primary colour)
         - Target Total Invoice Amount  (primary colour)
         - Difference (Source − Target) (green=0, red=negative, amber=positive)
         - Column name shown as a small pill label.
    3. Comparison Summary cards (Source Rows, Target Rows, Matched, etc.)

  Client-side fallback for existing saved reports (no invoice_summary field):
    If payload.report.invoice_summary is null (report saved before this fix),
    the frontend computes totals from full_comparison.rows:
      - Detects amount column from the first source_row that has data.
      - Detects amount column independently from the first target_row that has data
        (handles cases where source and target use different column names).
      - Sums source_row[amtCol] only for rows where source_row is non-empty
        (skips Added rows where source_row = {}).
      - Sums target_row[tgtAmtCol] only for rows where target_row is non-empty
        (skips Deleted rows where target_row = {}).

  Key code (client-side fallback):
    const sampleSrc = rows.find(r => r.source_row && Object.keys(r.source_row).length)?.source_row || {};
    const sampleTgt = rows.find(r => r.target_row && Object.keys(r.target_row).length)?.target_row || {};
    const amtKeywords = ['amount','amt','value','total','price','sum','debit','credit'];
    amtCol    = Object.keys(sampleSrc).find(k => amtKeywords.some(w => k.toLowerCase().includes(w)));
    tgtAmtCol = Object.keys(sampleTgt).find(k => amtKeywords.some(w => k.toLowerCase().includes(w)));
    srcTotal = rows.reduce((s, r) => {
      const keys = Object.keys(r.source_row || {});
      if (!keys.length) return s;
      const col = amtCol && keys.includes(amtCol) ? amtCol
                : keys.find(k => amtKeywords.some(w => k.toLowerCase().includes(w)));
      return s + (col ? parseAmt(r.source_row[col]) : 0);
    }, 0);
    tgtTotal = rows.reduce((s, r) => {
      const keys = Object.keys(r.target_row || {});
      if (!keys.length) return s;
      const col = tgtAmtCol && keys.includes(tgtAmtCol) ? tgtAmtCol
                : keys.find(k => amtKeywords.some(w => k.toLowerCase().includes(w)));
      return s + (col ? parseAmt(r.target_row[col]) : 0);
    }, 0);

  IMPACT:
  - New reconciliations: invoice_summary is computed server-side and stored in
    the diff JSON. EDA modal reads it directly.
  - Existing saved reports: client-side fallback computes totals from the
    full_comparison rows already in memory. No re-reconciliation needed.
  - Master data series: invoice section is never shown (no amount column
    detected, or isTransactional is false).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHANGE ENTRY #12
Date: 2025-08-03
Topic: Bug Fix — Target Invoice Total Showing $0.00 (Wrong Column Detection)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  After Entry #11, the Invoice Financial Summary showed correct Source Total
  but Target Total Invoice Amount was always $0.00.

ROOT CAUSE:
  The client-side fallback detected the amount column name from source_row
  keys, then used that same column name to look up values in target_row.
  In the transactional diff engine, matched/updated rows have both source_row
  and target_row populated with the original column names. However, the
  initial version of the fallback code was:

    tgtTotal = rows.reduce((s, r) =>
      s + (Object.keys(r.target_row || {}).length ? parseAmt(r.target_row[amtCol]) : 0), 0);

  This assumed target_row always uses the same column name as source_row.
  In practice, for rows where the target file had a differently-named amount
  column (or where the column name had a suffix from the merge), the lookup
  returned undefined → 0 for every row.

  Additionally, the original code did not detect the amount column from a
  sample target_row independently — it only sampled source_row.

FIX:
  FILE MODIFIED: frontend/src/App.jsx  [FIXED]

  - Added independent amount column detection from a sample target_row:
      const sampleTgt = rows.find(r => r.target_row && Object.keys(r.target_row).length)?.target_row || {};
      const tgtAmtCol = Object.keys(sampleTgt).find(k => amtKeywords.some(w => k.toLowerCase().includes(w)));

  - Target total now uses tgtAmtCol (detected from target_row) instead of
    assuming the same column name as source:
      tgtTotal = rows.reduce((s, r) => {
        const keys = Object.keys(r.target_row || {});
        if (!keys.length) return s;
        const col = tgtAmtCol && keys.includes(tgtAmtCol) ? tgtAmtCol
                  : keys.find(k => amtKeywords.some(w => k.toLowerCase().includes(w)));
        return s + (col ? parseAmt(r.target_row[col]) : 0);
      }, 0);

  - Per-row column lookup as final fallback: even if the sample-detected column
    name is not present in a specific row, each row independently searches for
    an amount-like key. This handles edge cases where column names vary per row
    (e.g. sparse data or mixed-schema exports).

  IMPACT:
  - Target Total Invoice Amount now correctly sums all target_row amounts.
  - Works regardless of whether source and target use the same or different
    column names for the invoice amount field.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHANGE ENTRY #13
Date: 2025-08-03
Topic: UI Cleanup — Remove Data Type Badges from EDA Modal
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  The EDA modal (Reconciliation EDA Report popup) showed two data type badges:
  1. Top-right header badge: "⚡ Transactional" or "Master Data" pill.
  2. Inside Comparison Summary section: "Transactional Data" or "Master Data" pill.

  These badges were not reliably reflecting the actual data type because:
  - The top-right badge was driven by isTransactional which depended on both
    payload.dataType AND arResult state — not purely the stored data type.
  - The inner badge was driven by the same isTransactional flag.
  - Users found the badges confusing since they sometimes showed "Master Data"
    for transactional files (when the series was created before the data_type
    field was properly stored).

  Decision: remove both badges entirely from the EDA modal rather than risk
  showing incorrect labels. The data type is already implied by the content
  shown (invoice totals appear for transactional, comparison summary for master).

FILES MODIFIED:
  frontend/src/App.jsx  [MODIFIED]

  Removed from EDA modal header (top-right):
    <span className={`pill ${payload.dataType === 'transactional' ? 'data-type-transactional' : 'data-type-master'}`}>
      {payload.dataType === 'transactional' ? '⚡ Transactional' : 'Master Data'}
    </span>

  Removed from Comparison Summary section (inside non-AR branch):
    <span className={`pill ${payload.dataType === 'transactional' ? 'data-type-transactional' : 'data-type-master'}`}>
      {payload.dataType === 'transactional' ? 'Transactional Data' : 'Master Data'}
    </span>

  IMPACT:
  - EDA modal header now shows only the Close button on the right side.
  - Comparison Summary section now shows only the Keys pill.
  - No incorrect "Master Data" label shown for transactional files.
  - The invoice financial summary section itself serves as the visual indicator
    that the data is transactional.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHANGE ENTRY #14
Date: 2025-08-03
Topic: Summary — Full EDA Modal Transactional Data Flow (End-to-End)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OVERVIEW:
  This entry documents the complete end-to-end flow for how the EDA modal
  now works for transactional data, combining all fixes from Entries #10–#13.

COMPLETE FLOW:

  1. USER UPLOADS TWO FILES (standard series flow, not AR):
     - User picks Source file and Target file in the Reconcile view.
     - Backend detects data_type via resolve_data_type() in app.py.
     - If transactional: calls transactional_difference_summary() which now
       also computes invoice_summary (amount column auto-detected, totals summed).
     - diff report stored as JSON with invoice_summary embedded.

  2. USER OPENS EDA MODAL (clicks "View EDA Report" on a day card):
     - Frontend reads payload = versionReports[edaDay].
     - payload.report contains the full diff JSON including invoice_summary.
     - payload.dataType = report.data_type = "transactional" or "master".

  3. EDA MODAL RENDERS:
     - isAR = !!(arResult?.summary)  — true only if AR run done this session.
     - isTransactional = payload.dataType === 'transactional' || isAR.

     Branch A — isTransactional && isAR (AR run was done):
       - 11-cell AR KPI strip (Source Records, Target Records, Matched Txns,
         Amount Mismatch, Only in Source/Target, Tier-2, Exceptions, Dup Keys).
       - AR Financial Summary: 3 invoice cards + 10 count cards.
       - Transaction Breakdown pie chart.

     Branch B — isTransactional && !isAR (standard transactional series):
       - 7-cell standard KPI strip (Total, Matched, Updated, Inserted,
         Missing, Duplicate, Quality).
       - Invoice Financial Summary section:
           Source Total Invoice Amount | Target Total Invoice Amount | Difference
           (computed from invoice_summary if present, else from full_comparison rows).
       - Comparison Summary cards (Source Rows, Target Rows, Matched, etc.).

     Branch C — !isTransactional (master data):
       - 7-cell standard KPI strip.
       - Comparison Summary cards only.
       - No invoice section.

  4. INVOICE TOTAL COMPUTATION PRIORITY:
     Priority 1 (server-side, new reports):
       payload.report.invoice_summary.source_invoice_total / target_invoice_total
     Priority 2 (client-side fallback, existing saved reports):
       Computed from payload.report.full_comparison.rows by:
       - Detecting amount column independently from source_row and target_row samples.
       - Summing only rows where that side has data (skipping Deleted/Added empties).
       - Per-row column lookup as final fallback for mixed-schema rows.

  KEY FILES:
    backend/app.py                  — transactional_difference_summary() + invoice_summary
    frontend/src/App.jsx            — EDA modal branching logic + client-side fallback

================================================================================
  END OF CHANGELOG
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FINAL SUMMARY — HOW THE SYSTEM WORKS NOW (as of 2025-08-03)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

RECONCILIATION APP — SHORT WORKING SUMMARY

1. UPLOAD & RECONCILE
   - User uploads Source + Target files on the Reconcile tab.
   - Backend auto-detects data type: "master" or "transactional".
   - If transactional: runs transactional_difference_summary() which computes
     row-level diffs AND invoice_summary (source total, target total, difference).
   - If master: runs standard difference_summary() (no invoice totals).
   - Results saved as diff JSON per version. Series stored in Postgres + file system.

2. IF BOTH FILES ARE TRANSACTIONAL (AR MODE)
   - Frontend auto-detects via /api/ar/detect-type on file pick.
   - Action button switches to "Run AR Reconcile".
   - AR engine (ar_reconcile.py) runs: maps columns canonically, groups by
     TxnNumber, matches exact then tier-2, splits exceptions/duplicates.
   - AR result stored in arResult state (not saved to disk).

3. EDA MODAL (View EDA Report button on day card)
   - Opens for any version in the day-by-day scoreboard.
   - Shows: KPI strip + financial summary + comparison cards.

   MASTER DATA path:
     - 7 KPI cells: Total, Matched, Updated, Inserted, Missing, Duplicate, Quality.
     - Comparison Summary cards: Source Rows, Target Rows, Matched, Added,
       Deleted, Renamed, Duplicates, Value Changes, Format Issues.
     - No invoice section.

   TRANSACTIONAL (standard series, no AR run):
     - 7 KPI cells (same as master).
     - Invoice Financial Summary: Source Total | Target Total | Difference.
       Computed from invoice_summary in report, or from full_comparison rows
       as fallback for older saved reports.
     - Comparison Summary cards below.

   TRANSACTIONAL + AR RUN DONE (arResult in state):
     - 11 AR KPI cells: Source/Target Records, Matched Txns, Amount Mismatch,
       Only in Source/Target, Tier-2, Exceptions, Dup Keys.
     - AR Financial Summary: 3 invoice cards + 10 count cards.
     - Transaction Breakdown pie chart.

4. AR RESULTS PANEL (inline on Reconcile tab after AR run)
   - Tabs: Summary | Matched | Disputed | Unmatched Src/Tgt | Tier-2 |
           Dup Keys Src/Tgt | Exceptions Src/Tgt.
   - Summary tab: 3 invoice cards (Source Total, Target Total, Difference) +
     10 count cards. Difference colour-coded green/red/amber.

5. KEY DESIGN DECISIONS
   - invoice_summary computed server-side for new reports; client-side fallback
     for existing saved reports (reads full_comparison rows).
   - Amount column auto-detected by keyword scan (amount/amt/value/total/price/
     sum/debit/credit) independently for source and target sides.
   - Data type badges removed from EDA modal (were unreliable; content itself
     implies the type).
   - AR result (arResult) is session-only state — not persisted to disk.
   - Standard series and AR reconcile are independent flows sharing the same UI.

================================================================================
  END OF CHANGELOG
================================================================================
